Cell["\<\
Double check with random numbers. We can home that series converge only when \
divide by determinant norm. (In general even that  could not be enough). \
Therefore we have to divide any MV by that norm. While sinh and cosh seems \
converge with smaller max coefficients, this is not the case for tanh! \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.819371128707596*^9, 3.819371135708658*^9}, {
  3.819944763706498*^9, 3.819944800698094*^9}, {3.819945030900075*^9, 
  3.819945072701333*^9}, {3.819945205130818*^9, 3.819945236248599*^9}, {
  3.8199453897729*^9, 3.819945669246696*^9}, {3.819946151723941*^9, 
  3.819946156853283*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"600b3173-8250-4fce-ac99-\
16b23a2234f2"],

Cell["\<\
We will use the same random numerical coefficients, since we want to do same \
computations with tanh/ctanh later\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.819371128707596*^9, 3.819371135708658*^9}, {
  3.819944763706498*^9, 3.819944800698094*^9}, {3.819945030900075*^9, 
